  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "version": "2.6.6",
   "params": [],
   "pos": [
    83,
    2
   ],
   "data": {
    "text": "HEMIOLA AUDIO: RAINY SUNDAY, GREY SKIES\n\nNothing here plays on a steady beat.\nRandom 1 fires triggers at an irregular pace. LFO 1 slowly speeds that pace up and down, and Random 1 also skips about a quarter of its triggers. Those triggers are the beat for Cycle Clock.\nCycle Clock counts them as a cycle. Its cycle trigger is patched back into its own CYCLE CV input in COUNT mode, so every lap it moves to the next of its 55 cycles (7, then 8, 9, 10 ...). The pattern of sections keeps changing.\nR&T 1 splits each irregular beat. Random 2 picks its DIVISION anew in every section, so the drops sometimes pitter quickly and sometimes barely fall.\nR&T 2 listens to the cycle's sections. Its DIVISION steps up by one every lap (COUNT mode) and wraps from 9 back to 1.\n\nSounds: rain drops (high sine pings, D minor pentatonic), glass bells, a slow pad whose 7-step chord sequence is clocked by the sections, soft pink-noise mist that breathes, fine rain patter, and a faint city hum. Two delays blur the drops, bells and pad into a wash.\n\nTry: lower the mist VCA level for a drier room; turn Random 1 PROB to 100 percent for a steadier pulse; set Cycle Clock CV mode to LEVEL to freeze the cycle; change the Quantizer notes to another scale."
   }
  }
 ],
